  "summary": "New T2D-focused frameworks and resources connect fine-mapped GWAS signals to tissue eQTLs, splicing, islet single-cell data and chromatin-defined cell types.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving GWAS loci to candidate effector genes and the cell contexts in which they act, with type 2 diabetes as a recurring test case. CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTL PIPs and allelic fold changes across five metabolic tissues. CELL-X carries T2D fine-mapped genes into islet single-cell atlases for beta-cell-relevant prioritization. A multi-layer colocalization study of 338 T2D signals extends beyond gene-level expression to GTEx adipose exon, transcript and splice-junction usage. EPIC2 ranks trait-relevant cell types by linking GWAS summary statistics to single-cell chromatin accessibility while modeling LD. On the resource side, CellColocDB applies coloc.abf across bulk, sorted-cell and single-cell data, and the IGVF Catalog integrates 657 variant-function datasets into a knowledge graph with APIs and an LLM interface. RapidGLM accelerates eQTL and count-regression analyses. A secondary strand covers spatial co-localization testing (spicyR v2, spatialFDA) and single-cell atlases.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
